Aerie-Purpose: Report a charging, full battery from navigator.getBattery() and raise no battery events while fingerprinting protection is on, so the real battery is no fingerprint surface (issue #120).
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/renderer/modules/battery/battery_manager.cc (DidUpdateData), third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/navigator_masking.h, third_party/blink/public/common/helium_noise/ (HeliumNoiseFeature::kNavigator), content/browser/helium_noise/noise_token_data.cc, third_party/blink/common/features.cc (kHeliumNoiseNavigator)
Aerie-Kind: hook

HeliumNoiseFeature::kNavigator is a new surface token, added the way hardening/0015 adds kScreen: a
session token in HeliumNoiseTokenData that GetTokens derives per site, and a renderer that receives
it only when protection is on for the site. "Token present" therefore means "protected here", and the
global switch and the per-site switch give the real values back without a renderer change. The new
feature kHeliumNoiseNavigator (on by default) switches the surface off for the Bench's negative
control. hardening/0022 uses the same token for the speech voices.

A protected window reads battery_status_ as charging, level 1, charging time 0 and discharging time
Infinity (the values in components/aerie_navigator_pins; they are also BatteryStatus's own defaults,
which is what a machine with no battery reports). BatteryManager::DidUpdateData replaces the status
the dispatcher delivered with that value before it compares the old and the new status, so the
real battery raises no chargingchange, levelchange, chargingtimechange or dischargingtimechange
event either. The decision (ShouldPinNavigatorForContext, in core/execution_context) is a window's
token, read the same way as ShouldMaskGpuInfoForContext. getBattery() is a window API only, so there
is no worker case.

navigator.languages needs no patch: Helium turns ReduceAcceptLanguage on
(helium/core/reduce-accept-language-headers.patch), and NavigatorLanguage::EnsureUpdatedLanguage then
reduces navigator.languages to the first entry, the same one the Accept-Language header carries. The
Bench check hardening_fingerprinting_navigator fails if that is lost.

